\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Representation of a finite-population Markov chain describing the stochastic evolution of two competing phenotypes A (yellow) and B (green). Each state represents a population composition, with transitions between neighboring states governed by the probabilities \(T_{i,j}\). The intermediate states are transient, allowing fluctuations in phenotype frequencies, whereas the boundary states \(p=0\) and \(p=1\) are absorbing, corresponding to the fixation of one phenotype and the extinction of the other, inspired by \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {nowakEvolutionaryDynamicsExploring2006}.}}{8}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:markovChains}{{1}{8}{Representation of a finite-population Markov chain describing the stochastic evolution of two competing phenotypes A (yellow) and B (green). Each state represents a population composition, with transitions between neighboring states governed by the probabilities \(T_{i,j}\). The intermediate states are transient, allowing fluctuations in phenotype frequencies, whereas the boundary states \(p=0\) and \(p=1\) are absorbing, corresponding to the fixation of one phenotype and the extinction of the other, inspired by \cite {nowakEvolutionaryDynamicsExploring2006}}{figure.1}{}}
