\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Schematic representation of the Moran process. At each step, in a finite population of $N$ individuals, an individual is selected for reproduction (duplication) with a probability proportional to its fitness (upper arrow), while another is chosen at random to die (lower arrow). The offspring of the first replaces the second, keeping the population size constant. This iterative process allows observation of how phenotypes spread or go extinct over time inspired by \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {nowakEvolutionaryDynamicsExploring2006}.}}{12}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:moranProcess}{{2}{12}{Schematic representation of the Moran process. At each step, in a finite population of $N$ individuals, an individual is selected for reproduction (duplication) with a probability proportional to its fitness (upper arrow), while another is chosen at random to die (lower arrow). The offspring of the first replaces the second, keeping the population size constant. This iterative process allows observation of how phenotypes spread or go extinct over time inspired by \cite {nowakEvolutionaryDynamicsExploring2006}}{figure.2}{}}
